{
  "spec": "fp2-agent-lifecycle-parity",
  "story": "ALR-1103",
  "note": "Extends the pinned tests/data/fp2_conformance.json corpus with full manifest-shaped afp2/dfp2o/efp2/cfp2 cases scoped to fp2's cross-runtime parity contract (docs/fingerprints/fp2.md: 'Comparability scope'). dfp2o/cfp2 carry no runtime field and MUST canonicalize identically regardless of input construction order (scope=cross_runtime). afp2/efp2 carry a mandatory runtime discriminator and are deterministic only WITHIN one runtime (scope=within_runtime_only): same-family cases with different 'runtime' values share source/bound content but MUST NOT digest equal -- asserting otherwise is this story's named failure mutation (PART1_CONTRACT_FREEZE_DRAFT.md:1148, mutation row 10). scope=preserve_unknown demonstrates the canonicalizer keeps a field none of the four fp2 algorithms name, rather than silently dropping it. scope=fail_closed demonstrates the opposite half: a value fp2 cannot represent fails the whole manifest closed. Markers @@NAN@@/@@LONE_SURROGATE@@ are substituted with the language's native unsupported value by each harness, matching tests/data/fp2_conformance.json. The top-level 'shared' section below names two kinds of content that is byte-identical across two or more cases purely incidentally to what each case tests -- never the part a case's name says it varies. A case references a shared fragment two ways, both resolved by the test loader (tests/test_fp2_agent_lifecycle_parity.py:_cases()) before anything touches the corpus: (1) inside 'value', a nested object of exactly {\"$shared\": \"<name>\"} is replaced with a deep copy of shared['<name>']; (2) at the case level, 'expected_ref': '<name>' replaces literal 'canonical'/'digest' fields with shared['<name>'].canonical / .digest. Every case that still carries 'value'/'canonical'/'digest' inline does so because that content is the actual point of the case, not boilerplate.",
